  m_Name: Vis
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  partName: Engine Mounting Bolts
  description: The Engine Mounting Bolts are located at the middle-center-center
    of the rocket engine and are made of a robust Vis material, which provides exceptional
    strength and resistance to fatigue. These large, complex-shaped bolts are responsible
    for securing the engine to the vehicle's structure, ensuring that the engine
    remains stable and aligned during operation. Notably, the engine mounting bolts
    are designed to withstand the intense vibrations and stresses generated by the
    engine's operation, making them a critical component of the engine's overall
    mounting system.
